  "stem": "A scientist models the number of cells in a sample \\(h\\) hours after the start of an experiment with the function \\(C(h) = 50(3)^{h}\\). According to the model, how many cells are in the sample 4 hours after the start of the experiment?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "4050"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Substitute \\(4\\) for \\(h\\): \\(C(4) = 50(3)^{4}\\).",
    "\\(3^{4} = 81\\), so \\(C(4) = 50 \\cdot 81 = 4{,}050\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "h = symbols('h')\nC = Lambda(h, 50*3**h)\nassert C(4) == 4050\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [C(4)]",
